/E (In 1986, I was living with my husband and children in Colorado Springs, Colorado, and my parents joined us there so that they could be closer to me and their grandchildren. A year later, Rabbi Mendy Teitelbaum came to the area as the Chabad emissary, and my father developed a close relationship with him. Rabbi Teitelbaum knew that if he was short a man for the minyan, or if he needed help with a particular mitzvah, he could always count on my father.)
